#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:0
msgid ""
"Turn on Hover Click to click or drag by holding the pointer over a control, "
"and adjust the delay and motion threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr "話題：無障礙功能"

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:11
msgid "Simulate clicking by hovering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:13
msgid ""
"You can click or drag simply by hovering your mouse pointer over a control "
"or object on the screen. This is useful if you find it difficult to move the "
"mouse and click at the same time. This feature is called **Hover Click** or "
"**Dwell Click**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:15
msgid ""
"When Hover Click is enabled, you can move your mouse pointer over a control, "
"let go of the mouse, and then wait for a while before the button will be "
"clicked for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:17
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:18
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:19
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Pointing & Clicking` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:20
msgid ""
"In the {guilabel}`Click Assist` section, enable the {guilabel}`Hover Click` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:22
msgid ""
"The {guilabel}`Hover Click` window will open, and will stay above all of "
"your other windows. You can use this to choose what sort of click should "
"happen when you hover. For example, if you select {guilabel}`Secondary "
"Click`, you will right-click when you hover. After you double-click, right-"
"click, or drag, you will be automatically returned to clicking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:24
msgid ""
"When you hover your mouse pointer over a button and do not move it, it will "
"gradually change color. When it has fully changed color, the button will be "
"clicked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:26
msgid ""
"Adjust the {guilabel}`Delay` setting to change how long you have to hold the "
"mouse pointer still before clicking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:28
msgid ""
"You do not need to hold the mouse perfectly still when hovering to click. "
"The pointer is allowed to move a little bit and will still click after a "
"while. If it moves too much, however, the click will not happen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/simulate-clicking-by-hovering.md:30
msgid ""
"Adjust the {guilabel}`Motion Threshold` setting to change how much the "
"pointer can move and still be considered to be hovering."
msgstr ""
